eral Education Policies How to Apply Steps to Apply Dates and Deadlines Visit Virtual Tour Graduate Student Tours Plan Your Visit Request Information Meet Your Counselor After Admission Orientation Orientation Steps Placement Tests Youth & Pre-College Programs Cost of Attendance Net Price Calculator Reduced Tuition for Out of State Students Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Accept Your Aid Manage Your Aid Scholarships Apply for Scholarships Manage & Renew Your Scholarship Manage External Scholarships Loans Federal Loans Health Professions Loans Private Loans Short-Term Loans Grants IU Indianapolis Pledge Federal Pell Federal Supplemental Frank O’Bannon Child of Disabled Veteran National Guard Supplemental Work-Study Pay Your Bill Make a Payment Deposits and Prepayments Receive Your Refund Tax Information Tuition Disputes Participate in Research Opportunities for Undergraduate Students Opportunities for Graduate Students Volunteer for a Research Study Research Initiatives Community Engaged Research Centers & Institutes IU Indianapolis Faculty Academic Advising Schedule an Appointment Academic Support & Tutoring Libraries Educational Success Programs Groups Student Support Services Career Services & Jobs Explore Careers Fall Career Week Health & Wellness Technology & Tools Recruit IU Indy Students Athletics and Recreation Student Organizations Events Housing Dining IUPUI Transition to IU Indianapolis IU Indianapolis Leadership Meet IU Indianapolis Leadership Chancellor Updates Request an Appearance State of the Campus Campus Initiatives History Strategic Plan Goals Honors and Awards Chancellor’s Medallion Student Awards Visit Apply Home Student Support Career Services & Jobs Explore Careers Clarify your career interests As you explore pathways and gain experience, you may discover new interests or confirm your chosen career field. Learn steps to take while still a student to prepare for your career. Prepare for your career Get part-time work experience Working on or off campus helps you develop skills and experience, build your network, and earn a position. Learn through service Career exposure comes in many forms, including through community service, volunteering, and civic engagement. Conduct research Grow your resume, uncover insights, and advance your knowledge by working on a faculty-led research project. Gain internship experience Get professional experience in a career field you’re considering. Not only will you become more career-ready; you may also earn academic credit and get paid for your work. Join a student organization Develop leadership skills, learn more about yourself, and explore different areas of interest. Attend on-campus career events Whether it’s a career fair, networking event, or career development workshop, these live events can set you up for success. Explore careers with these resources Understand occupation outlooks The Occupational Outlook Handbook from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics offers career information on duties, education and training, pay, and outlook for hundreds of occupations. Connect knowledge and skills to occupations Use O*NET to search careers by your preferred interests, and discover what skills and education are needed to achieve your goals. Unlock opportunities by major Ever wonder what you can do with your IU major? Discover job titles, salary information, and places you could work. Take a course With so many major and career options, it can be challenging to choose a path. Our 1-credit 8-week Career Connections course can help you figure it out. Search for course offerings. Conduct an informational interview Hearing from professionals in your chosen career field can uncover rich insights—and you’ll build your network while you’re at it! Ask your career services office to help connect you. Shadow a professional Spend some time getting an insider’s view of what it’s like to work in a certain career field. Your career services office can help connect you with people to shadow. Social media links x facebook instagram youtube linkedin Accessibility College Scorecard Open to All Privacy Notice Required disclosures Copyright © The Trustees of Indiana University"
    },
