on Policies How to Apply Steps to Apply Dates and Deadlines Visit Virtual Tour Graduate Student Tours Plan Your Visit Request Information Meet Your Counselor After Admission Orientation Orientation Steps Placement Tests Youth & Pre-College Programs Cost of Attendance Net Price Calculator Reduced Tuition for Out of State Students Financial Aid Apply for Financial Aid Accept Your Aid Manage Your Aid Scholarships Apply for Scholarships Manage & Renew Your Scholarship Manage External Scholarships Loans Federal Loans Health Professions Loans Private Loans Short-Term Loans Grants IU Indianapolis Pledge Federal Pell Federal Supplemental Frank O’Bannon Child of Disabled Veteran National Guard Supplemental Work-Study Pay Your Bill Make a Payment Deposits and Prepayments Receive Your Refund Tax Information Tuition Disputes Participate in Research Opportunities for Undergraduate Students Opportunities for Graduate Students Volunteer for a Research Study Research Initiatives Community Engaged Research Centers & Institutes IU Indianapolis Faculty Academic Advising Schedule an Appointment Academic Support & Tutoring Libraries Educational Success Programs Groups Student Support Services Career Services & Jobs Explore Careers Fall Career Week Health & Wellness Technology & Tools Recruit IU Indy Students Athletics and Recreation Student Organizations Events Housing Dining IUPUI Transition to IU Indianapolis IU Indianapolis Leadership Meet IU Indianapolis Leadership Chancellor Updates Request an Appearance State of the Campus Campus Initiatives History Strategic Plan Goals Honors and Awards Chancellor’s Medallion Student Awards Visit Apply Home Student Support Career Services & Jobs Fall Career Week Hone your career interests and skills Discover career paths, network with employers, and get career-ready during Fall Career Week. View the calendar Prepare for your career Whether it’s your first semester or last, you can benefit from Fall Career Week. Held as part of National Career Development Week each November, Fall Career Week offers opportunities to: Learn about career paths and the majors that will get you where you want to go. Develop skills for job-searching, such as how to prepare for an interview or negotiate a salary. Explore and plan for internships. Network with employers and professionals in a variety of career fields. Have your resume or LinkedIn profile reviewed. Get job-ready with a professional headshot or clothes from Hire Attire . Visit an actual employer during a Field Trip Friday (registration required). Fall Career Week by the numbers 40+ events to help you become career-ready 15-minute consultations for LinkedIn and resume reviews 700 student participants 30+ employer participants Career events for all students Fall Career Week is presented by the Division of Undergraduate Education and the Career Services Council, in partnership with each school. Events are open to all IU Indianapolis students, with many schools hosting events for students interested in specific career fields. View the calendar Join us for 2026 Fall Career Week, November 9-13! IU Indianapolis Academic and Career Development Taylor Hall, 3004 815 W Michigan St Indianapolis , IN 46202 USA +1-317-274-4856 advising@iu.edu Social media links x facebook instagram youtube linkedin Accessibility College Scorecard Open to All Privacy Notice Required disclosures Copyright © The Trustees of Indiana University"
